  - [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m + [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m — a separate Node entry point ([38;5;153mgreet[39m), also console-logging.
  - [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m has no dependencies, no scripts, no test setup.

  Two things stand out before we design anything. First, these are two different runtimes — a browser bundle and a Node
  script — and "add logging" means something quite different in each (browser logs need shipping somewhere to be
  debuggable in production; Node logs can go to stdout and be collected). Second, the one real flow in the app is a
  login form, so the logging design has to answer up front what happens to usernames and passwords — the current code
  already logs the username on every attempt.

